  """
// Theorem 7.2 (Upward Propagation).
// Incoherence at a component layer propagates upward to any
// emergent shape whose coherence depends on that component.
// The propagation is conditional: it occurs if and only if the
// emergent shape's structure requires coherent input from the
// affected component.
//
// If A's incoherence arises, the contact shape R becomes incoherent.
// Whether D survives depends on D's structure: if D can tolerate
// removing R from its context, D persists. If D depends on R for
// coherent transformation, D inherits the incoherence.
//
// Derives from: theory.fractal, theory.coherence.contact-is-shape
  """
